        "The firm maximises profit where marginal revenue equals marginal cost, provided marginal cost is rising. Below that output, an extra unit adds more to revenue than to cost, so expanding pays; beyond it, each unit costs more than it earns, so contraction pays. Profit is total revenue minus total cost, and normal profit is treated as a cost of enterprise. In {S}, applying the equality, and stating the rising-marginal-cost condition, is the standard route to full marks.",
