        "Street food sellers and hair salons in any Nigerian city are monopolistic competitors: many sellers, similar but differentiated services, easy entry, normal profits in the long run. Their signage, recipes and customer care are product differentiation in action. In {S}, such familiar markets supply the everyday evidence that makes structure classification questions easy to argue.",
