        "The CBN has pushed payments modernisation: the Treasury Single Account consolidated government balances from 2015, the cashless policy charges fees on large cash withdrawals, agent banking spread services to unbanked areas, and instant transfers became routine through NIBSS rails. The eNaira joined this stack in 2021, and financial inclusion has climbed as USSD codes reach customers without branches. In {S}, linking each innovation to a function of money or a banking problem it solves keeps the answer analytical.",
