        "Fiscal policy is the use of government spending, taxation and borrowing to influence aggregate demand, output, employment and prices. Expansionary fiscal policy raises spending or cuts taxes to fight recession; contractionary policy does the reverse to cool inflation. Fiscal tools also redistribute income and steer resources to roads, schools and power. In {S}, fiscal policy acts on the expenditure side of the economy directly, in contrast with monetary policy's indirect route through interest and credit.",
