        "Direct taxes fall on persons and firms who bear them, income tax, company tax, capital gains; indirect taxes fall on goods and services and can be shifted to buyers, VAT, customs duties, excises. Direct taxes can be finely graduated by ability to pay but invite evasion; indirect taxes are easy to collect at source but regressive, taking a larger share of a poor household's income. In {S}, classifying a levy and stating one merit and one defect earns the marks.",
